.TH DCS 1 "2026-10" "Ducky Can Shoot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dcs - scan a USB medium for malware, archive it, upload it and email the verdict
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dcs
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ducky Can Shoot
triages removable media.  It reads a medium, scans every file with ClamAV (when it
is installed) and a built-in heuristic engine aimed at USB attacks, archives the
medium into one image, uploads that image to a free host and sends the verdict by
email, including the download link when the medium is safe.
.PP
If a threat is found the archive and upload stages are skipped: nothing found on
the medium ever leaves the machine.
.PP
Started without a command,
.B dcs
opens the graphical interface, which runs the same pipeline as the command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Configuration file to use instead of the per-user default.
.TP
.B \-\-log-level LEVEL
DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dcs gui [\-\-device NODE] [\-\-autorun]
Start the graphical interface, optionally on a medium and running the job.
.TP
.B dcs devices [\-\-json]
List the removable media that are attached.
.TP
.B dcs scan PATH [\-\-engines IDS] [\-\-json]
Scan a path and report the findings.
.TP
.B dcs run \-\-device NODE [\-\-to ADDRESS] [\-\-yes]
Run the whole job: scan, archive, upload, email.
.TP
.B dcs watch [\-\-start|\-\-stop|\-\-status|\-\-test]
Watch for media that are plugged in and react the way the configuration says;
.B \-\-start
puts a watcher in the background, which is what the desktop autostart entry does.
.TP
.B dcs doctor [\-\-smtp] [\-\-json]
Check the environment, the engines and the configuration.
.TP
.B dcs config show|set|init|path
Inspect, change or create the configuration.
.TP
.B dcs install\-clamav [\-\-dry-run]
Install the optional ClamAV engine with the system package manager.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The medium is clean.
.TP
.B 1
Suspicious or infected.
.TP
.B 2
The run failed, was cancelled, or could not be evaluated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dcs/config.toml
Per-user configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/dcs/config.toml
System wide defaults, when present.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dcs
Archives, reports and work files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/dcs/watch.log
What the background watcher did.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/ducky-can-shoot/ .
